title: no_cpan = 1 without docker_image leaves the dist without a Releaser
updated: 2026-10-25T01:50:04Z
---

With `no_cpan = 1` the bundle removes `UploadToCPAN` from `@Basic` (`GETTY.pm:1159-1160`) and adds nothing in its place. `Dist::Zilla::Dist::Builder::release` croaks `you can't release without any Releaser plugins` before anything else runs (Dist::Zilla 6.037, `Dist/Zilla/Dist/Builder.pm:583`). So a private dist configured with nothing but `[@Author::GETTY] no_cpan = 1` cannot run `dzil release` at all: no `NextRelease`, no tag, no version bump, no `InstallRelease`. `GitHub::CreateRelease` and `InstallRelease` are AfterRelease plugins, not Releasers.

It only works when the dist brings its own Releaser: `docker_image` (Docker::API is one) or a hand-added `[Run::Release]` (sunriser does that). citiai-core's dist.ini has neither.

Suggestion, untested: add `[FakeRelease]` when `no_cpan` is set and no Docker default is wired, so the release flow (changelog, tag, bump, push) works for private dists out of the box. Document it at `=head2 no_cpan` (`GETTY.pm:266-271`), which today only says that `UploadToCPAN` is disabled.

Related and equally unguarded, not used by any fleet dist today (grep over all dist.ini): `Test::ChangesHasContent` is added unconditionally (`GETTY.pm:1257`), but with `no_changes = 1` the version heading is blanked (`NextRelease.format = ''`, `:1381`) and on the `task`/`manual_version` path there is no `NextRelease` at all (`:1391-1395`), so the generated `xt/release/changes_has_content.t` cannot find a heading for the version and the release tests fail. Worth one test each before somebody needs those paths.

